[step] Independent core-hold and neutral-Wago locating planes: the retained core foot ends at X−43.60; the fitted Wago half-well ends at X−44.45. The 0.85 mm separation belongs to the two mating interfaces.
alternatives: Extending the core foot to the well enters the connector pocket; moving the pocket plane changes its purchased-body clearance and capture. The core-hold lanes remain the lid bearing lanes.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-back-top.step
click: x=-44.450 y=459.900 z=270.200

[sliver] Functional snap-seat catch bearings: the 0.85 mm horizontal face is the cap’s 0.60 mm engagement plus 0.25 mm running allowance. The spring walls and seat stock retain their 3 mm section. The square bearing captures the ASSE, Pisco, regulator or meter cap after insertion. Tree(auto)/Default approaches through the empty snap mouth before hardware installation; physical cleanup and spring life are not established by geometry.
alternatives: Sloping the bearing provides a withdrawal ramp; filling beneath it occupies the spring-hook path. A 3 mm reach needs another 2.15 mm of spring travel and wider matching pockets. Thickening the vertical wall does not enlarge this horizontal bearing.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-back-top.step
