[ceiling] Fitted meter housing and snap profiles: the flat faces bound the complete housing flange, screw bosses, lead exit and cap hook, including the 16 mm aft installation sweep and 0.5 mm axial variation. They are the purchased-body and working-catch boundaries of one east-wall seat. Tree(auto)/Default reaches them through the empty west/fore opening before the meter is installed; geometric access does not establish easy support removal.
alternatives: Filling or corbelling into these faces enters the housing/insertion sweep or cap-hook path. Sloping the catch changes retention; shortening the housing pocket spends the required complete envelope.
